==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Extremely high damage, especially for a first sea sword.
* Good for grinding because of multi-target skills and AoE.
* Low mastery requirements.
* Both moves deal AoE damage.
* Decent M1 overall.
* Both attacks can be used in very quick succession.
* Easy to upgrade because the materials are pretty easy to get.
*Very good for sea events, as all the moves deal massive damage to [[Sea Beasts]] and boats in Ship raids.
* Useful against [[Terrorshark]]s due to massive damage and decent range,  allowing the user to attack the terrorshark from a safe distance.
*Great for PvP due to high damage output

|'''[Z] Wind Breaker'''
* Decent range.
* Can be used to knock back players.

|'''[X] Quake Sphere'''
* Can be used to trap players.
* Decent range.
* V2 can [[break Instinct]].
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* No stunning moves.
* Ground based moves with slow projectiles.
* Really hard to get V2 if below Lv. 700.
* Slow M1 speed.
* Doesn't work very well in the air.
* Has an above-average cost in the [[First Sea]].
* Last attack of a M1 cannot hit when in transformed [[Buddha]] form.

|'''[Z] Wind Breaker'''
* Does not stun enemies.
* Very easy to Instinct trick without prior usage of X.

|'''[X] Quake Sphere'''
* V1 form is difficult to hit in PvP.
* V2 form does not instantly deal full damage.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Bisento has one of [[Quake]]'s old abilities (Quake Sphere) as one of its moves.
* Bisento also shares it´s price with [[Quake]], at {{Money|1,000,000}}.
* The Bisento has the second highest damage per click in the game. (The first being [[Triple Dark Blade]] and third being [[True Triple Katana]].)
* Bisento, [[Dark Blade]], [[Katana]], and [[Cutlass]] received an animation update in [[Updates/17.2|Update 17.2]].
* Bisento is the most expensive [[sword]] in the [[First Sea]].
* Bisento, [[Dark Blade]], [[Saber]], and [[Pole]] are the only four swords to have a V2.
* Before [[Update 24]], if the player activated an auto-clicker right as the impact effect appeared, there was a chance the sword would have double its range.
* Bisento V2’s {{Ability|Z}} is similar to [[Mammoth]]'s {{Ability|Mammoth|Z}} but smaller.
* For some reason, the fourth M1 animation doesn't work in [[Buddha]] transformation which makes grinding easier.
* The Bisento is the only sword that has a level requirement to be purchased from a dealer NPC.
* Bisento is considered the weaker version of Dark Blade by many players.

